Wizards are awesome for beginners for several reasons:

In the beginning, you get guarenteed magic resistance, and some
starting items from a wide variety.  With some daggers from the
gnomish mines and liberal use of Elbereth and your pet, you can
survive the early game.  An early wish (not that hard) for SDSM makes
it easier by giving the wizard an awesome boost to AC and reflection.
If they find a coaligned altar, it means Magicbane and win by spamming
Elbereth, because it means no melee for the wizard.

Ranged > Melee for wizards.  1. It deals more damage, 2. Monsters
generally suck at ranged

Running around bashing things like a barbarian is just asking for
trouble and a YASD.

For newbie wizards, the advice I can give is this, use your magic
sparingly.  Use it at the right moment for great effect.  Know which
spells rock (charm monster).

After you get the guarenteed uber Eye of the Aethiopica, you have just
won the game. Now go to the castle, get polymorph.  Abuse it to buff
yourself to an ultimate form and get the items you want.  Then win.

Wizards win if you know how to abuse them.


